# This repository is an archive of long-form documents rather than source
# code. These attributes keep git and GitHub's tooling fast when working
# with it:
#
# 1. Mark every document as "documentation" so GitHub's language-detection
#    statistics don't scan the full multi-hundred-KB contents of each file.
# 2. Disable line-by-line diffing for the largest documents (500KB+, some
#    with 6000+ character lines). These are edited/replaced as whole
#    documents, not line-by-line like code, so computing a textual diff on
#    every push/PR is wasted work that also slows down `git diff`,
#    `git blame`, and GitHub's PR "Files changed" rendering.

